# Third-party libraries installed for extensions (not part of this submission)
# MedSAM was cloned and pip-installed locally to run Extension C (foundation model
# comparison). It is its own separate Git repository (has its own .git folder) and
# contains a 357MB checkpoint that GitHub will reject outright (>100MB hard limit)
# see README.md "Enabling the foundation-model extension" for how a marker can set
# this up themselves. Only this project's own small, real results from running it
# (outputs/medsam_vs_unet_comparison.csv, outputs/figures/extension_medsam_comparison.png)
# are committed.
MedSAM/

# Large / regenerable artefacts
# Trained model weights (outputs/unet_bcedice.pt, ~7.5 MB) and all other
# results in outputs/ ARE committed to this repository on purpose, so the
# marker can see real results without re-running the notebook. If you retrain
# locally and want git to ignore your new local copies instead, uncomment:
# outputs/unet_bcedice.pt

